{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794436704268837293,"compiled_state":{"alias":"successive-deceptive-xiphias","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"702fb4cc30c3348f99509d9bd02ff9306aa4c8f1225f3913f1504e8dadb2303a","event_uuid":"2528df38-e4e6-460f-a3a5-5f136253101b","position":{"commit_sha":"ce557abf9e0797187bae28b2553002a26c2e41b6","position":"1794436618751044517-2528df38-e4e6-460f-a3a5-5f136253101b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"075c43c9c34130897aa472715bfe498aca8ef737b7f00a270709b671a3099297","event_uuid":"5e51df95-4288-4d0d-8fa6-00db5348f2d9","position":{"commit_sha":"30ab799ed11b45afb1121f8412f1de7e57bce917","position":"1794436704268837292-5e51df95-4288-4d0d-8fa6-00db5348f2d9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794436618751044517,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5e51df95-4288-4d0d-8fa6-00db5348f2d9","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"51e0-5038-bf00-4653"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nAfter bug `nickelic-lazuline-gonolek` (Gerrit 3351), the tickets store no longer runs `git gc` on any path:\n- Every bounded git child runs with `maintenance.auto=false` and `gc.auto=0`.\n- The explicit write-locked step runs only `commit-graph`, `loose-objects` and `incremental-repack`.\n\nThat was deliberate. On the 1.07M-object production clone, `gc --auto` took 133.9 s and a full repack took 605.6 s, both past the step's 120 s bound. But it has two consequences:\n- Nothing ever prunes unreachable objects, such as the leftovers of failed writes, abandoned merges and compaction.\n- Nothing ever expires reflogs. The production `.git/logs/HEAD` was 4.5 MB on 2026-11-11.\n\nGrowth is slow. The production clone held about 1,800 unreachable loose objects older than 2 weeks after 2.5 months of operation. Even so, the growth is unbounded.\n\nTwo docs still describe the old posture:\n- `docs/concurrency.md`, in the caveat paragraph: \"keeps auto-gc ENABLED\" and \"It reclaims loose/pack growth on its own\".\n- `docs/scale-envelope.md`: stock `git gc` runs in the foreground of the write command and handles packing.\n\n## Why this is separate\n\nChange 3351 is at the 150-line bug-fix size floor. Its diff covers the incident: the stranded lock, and orphaned gc work running outside the write lock. This ticket covers the long-horizon reclamation policy, which needs a cadence decision. Options include an out-of-band `git maintenance run --task=gc` under the write lock on a schedule (the ADR 0051 escape hatch), `--task=reflog-expire` on newer git, or `--task=gc` gated by its own threshold.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Unreachable objects and reflog entries on the tickets store are reclaimed on some bounded cadence that never runs outside the write lock, or a recorded decision accepts unbounded growth with its measured rate.\n- [ ] `docs/concurrency.md` and `docs/scale-envelope.md` describe the current maintenance posture.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"29b8-8d86-af5b-4608","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Tickets store never prunes unreachable objects or expires reflogs after implicit gc was disabled; two docs still describe foreground auto-gc","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2528df38-e4e6-460f-a3a5-5f136253101b","5e51df95-4288-4d0d-8fa6-00db5348f2d9"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794436704268837293,"uuid":"af17ebf4-3755-4125-bbe5-9d91a0a306aa"}